      "description": "T. Rowe Price Dynamic Emerging Markets Bond ETF is an actively managed exchange-traded fund that seeks income and capital appreciation by investing primarily in debt securities issued by governments, government agencies, supranational organizations, and companies in emerging markets. The fund normally invests at least 80% of its net assets in emerging-market debt and may invest in both sovereign and corporate bonds across Latin America, Asia, Europe, Africa, and the Middle East. It may invest in securities of any credit rating, including below-investment-grade and defaulted debt. The ETF trades on Nasdaq under the ticker TDEM.",
